# Reach the Mnemonic Debugger on the serial console at 2400 baud, load Domain/OS
# from it, and take C164's route from the `)` prompt to a shell and `lcnode`.
#
# 2400 is not a search: the boot PROM's own autobaud table (FINDINGS.md C240)
# maps the shape a 2400 terminal's `0D` makes at its 2000-baud receiver to
# CSR $88 -- 2400, the sender's own rate -- so the negotiation closes. A 9600
# terminal's `0D` reads as $FE there, which the table answers with 4800, and
# the third character the firmware needs is then misread (000008C8's
# `cmp.b #$d, d1` / `bne.w $752`).
expect MD7C
# **Wait for the prompt, not the banner.** MD prints `\r\n>` *after* its sign-on
# and reads and discards whatever is typed while it is still printing -- the same
# type-ahead handling `md-keyboard-console-recipe` records for the keyboard
# console. A script that sent on the banner alone lost its first character: a
# two-node run received `DI W` as `I W` and `EX DOMAIN_OS` as `EMAIN_OS`.
expect >
send DI W\r
expect >
send EX DOMAIN_OS\r
expect )
send SH\r
expect login:
send user\r
expect Password
send \r
expect $
send /com/lcnode\r
